<title>USA: NovaCare to name president as CEO - WSJ.</title>
<headline>NovaCare to name president as CEO - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>NovaCare Inc is expected to announce today that it has named its president and chief operating officer to the post of chief executive officer, the Wall Street Journal said in Tuesday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>Timothy Foster would be appointed CEO, succeeding John Foster who would remain chairman, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The two Fosters were not related, the paper said.</p>
<p>NovaCare was expected to name James McLane, 58, formerly CEO of Aetna Health Plans and an executive vice president of Aetna Life &amp; Casualty Corp, as president and COO, the Journal said.</p>
<p>--New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
